<title>USA: Cooper sees $45 mln Q2 gain from Kirsch sale.</title>
<headline>Cooper sees $45 mln Q2 gain from Kirsch sale.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cooper Industries Inc  said Friday that it expects to realize a second quarter after-tax gain of $45 million from the sale of its  Kirsch drapery hardware and custom window business to Newell Co.</p>
<p>The company said the sale closed today.</p>
<p>Cooper added that some of the proceeds will be used to reduce its debt and possibly, for acquisitions. But the company said that some portion of the gain may be offset by certain ongoing restructuring costs.</p>
<p>Cooper Industries, with 1996 revenues of $5.3 billion, is a diversified, worldwide manufacturer of electrical products, tools and hardware, and automotive products.</p>
</text>
